Jenkins Build Triggers: Beyond Webhooks

Webhooks are a common way to trigger Jenkins jobs, but they’re not the only option. Jenkins supports multiple trigger types to automate builds.

Other Triggers Include:
- SCM Polling – Jenkins checks your repo at intervals (e.g., every 5 minutes).
- Scheduled Builds – Use cron syntax for nightly or weekly jobs.
- Remote Triggers – Trigger jobs via an external system using a tokenized URL.
- Upstream/Downstream Jobs – Automatically trigger jobs when another completes.

These options give you flexibility—ideal when webhooks aren’t available or when you need time-based or chained executions.
